            "content": "## 1. Honest baseline before anything changes\n\n- [ ] 1.1 Extend `apps/api/src/search/chat/eval/dataset.ts` with genuinely inflected Russian and Spanish queries (case-marked and conjugated forms that do **not** reuse the fixture's surface word forms) in the recorded — not floored — categories, and verify `pnpm --filter api test:integration` still passes with the existing floors untouched\n- [ ] 1.2 Run `RUN_SEARCH_EVAL=1` and rewrite `apps/api/src/search/chat/eval/BASELINE.md` with the true pre-embedding numbers, verifying the new inflected rows are recorded and the \"Reading it\" note states what they measure\n\n## 2. Database image floor\n\n- [ ] 2.1 Move `compose.yaml` to a digest-pinned `pgvector/pgvector:pg17`, keeping the refresh-command comment convention, and verify `pnpm db:reset && pnpm db:migrate && pnpm db:provision-rls` completes on the new image\n- [ ] 2.2 Move the Testcontainers image in `apps/api/vitest.integration.global-setup.mts` and the Playwright default in `playwright.config.ts` (`E2E_DB_PG_IMAGE`) to the same digest-pinned image, and verify `pnpm --filter api test:integration` passes unchanged\n- [ ] 2.3 Update CI Postgres service images to match, and verify the workflow's database-backed jobs pass on a pushed branch\n- [ ] 2.4 Document pgvector as a self-host deployment requirement in `README.md` and `apps/api/AGENTS.md`, and verify `pnpm lint:markdown` passes\n\n## 3. Schema and isolation\n\n- [ ] 3.1 Add the `vector` extension and the model-binding ledger table via `drizzle-kit`, and verify migration succeeds as the non-superuser owner role on a fresh database\n- [ ] 3.2 Add `search_chat_embeddings` (PK `(document_id, model_key)`, `document_id` FK cascade to `search_chat_documents`, denormalized `owner_user_id`/`chat_id`, `embedded_content_hash`, dimensionless `vector`, `created_at`) with `.enableRLS()` and the `FOR ALL` owner policy, and verify the generated migration matches the schema\n- [ ] 3.3 Hand-append `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` to the migration, record the exception in the `apps/api/AGENTS.md` migration exception ledger with its regeneration requirement, and verify `migration-journal` checks pass\n- [ ] 3.4 Write `search-embeddings-rls.integration.test.ts` asserting no row is readable as another user's identity and as the empty identity, including for a `visibility = 'public'` chat, and verify it fails when the policy is removed\n- [ ] 3.5 Assert deletion propagation: deleting a chat, and reindexing away a document, both leave no embedding row — verified by integration test\n\n## 4. Configuration surface\n\n- [ ] 4.1 Add the optional `embeddingModels[]` array and per-corpus intended-model setting to the config schema, referencing `providers[].id`, and verify the published JSON Schema rejects a dangling provider reference, a duplicate id, and a non-positive `dimensions` at boot naming the offending entry\n- [ ] 4.2 Implement the binding ledger check — first use of a key records its binding; a declared key whose binding differs is rejected at load naming the key and changed field — and verify with a unit test for both the first-use and redefinition paths\n- [ ] 4.3 Verify an instance with no `embeddingModels` boots clean, creates no queue, issues no provider request, and leaves search behavior identical, asserted by test\n- [ ] 4.4 Verify a resolved embedding-provider credential appears in no log, error, or diagnostic, asserted by test alongside the existing provider redaction tests\n\n## 5. Provider boundary\n\n- [ ] 5.1 Add the corpus-agnostic `EmbeddingBackend` interface (`embedQuery`, `embedDocuments`) and injection token to `apps/api/src/search/core/`, and verify the module dependency direction is preserved by the existing structure tests\n- [ ] 5.2 Implement the OpenAI-compatible adapter reusing an existing `providers[]` connection, applying asymmetric document/query prefixes when configured, and verify with unit tests against a stubbed endpoint including the keyless-provider case\n- [ ] 5.3 Validate every returned vector for registered dimensions and finite values before it leaves the adapter, and verify a wrong-length and a non-finite vector are both rejected with nothing persisted\n- [ ] 5.4 Correlate results to requests by explicit `(model_key, document_id, content_hash)` key, and verify a reordered and a partial provider response are matched correctly with unmatched results discarded\n\n## 6. Pipeline\n\n- [ ] 6.1 Define `SEARCH_EMBED_QUEUE` in `apps/api/src/search/reindex-queues.ts` with `policy: 'stately'` and per-chat `singletonKey`, and verify the queue-contract test covers its parse function\n- [ ] 6.2 Enqueue embed work from the reindex worker **after** the rebuild transaction commits, and from the sweep for chats whose coverage lags, and verify by integration test that a burst of writes to one chat collapses to one pending embed job\n- [ ] 6.3 Implement the embed worker: resolve the chat's documents under `runAs(owner)`, select those missing or hash-mismatched for the intended model, embed, and insert conditionally on the hash still matching — verified by integration test end to end\n- [ ] 6.4 Verify the hash guard by test: edit a message between request and persist, and delete the chat between request and persist; in both cases nothing is written and no deleted content is representable\n- [ ] 6.5 Verify a failing or unreachable backend leaves lexical indexing, search, and turn completion unaffected, with affected documents still queued — asserted by integration test\n\n## 7. Backfill and observability\n\n- [ ] 7.1 Add the operator-invocable backfill over existing documents, and verify a second run against a covered corpus issues no provider request and writes no row\n- [ ] 7.2 Expose per-chat embedding coverage alongside the existing `indexed_at`, and verify an operator can distinguish complete coverage from lag during a partial backfill\n- [ ] 7.3 Implement coverage-gated corpus activation: the intended model is served only once coverage is complete, incomplete coverage is a logged runtime state and never a boot failure — verified by test for both states\n\n## 8. Proof of no observable change\n\n- [ ] 8.1 Run the full relevance eval on a fully embedded corpus and verify `BASELINE.md` metrics are byte-identical to task 1.2's recorded numbers\n- [ ] 8.2 Run `pnpm --filter api test`, `pnpm --filter api test:integration`, `pnpm --filter api lint`, and `pnpm --filter api build`, and verify all pass\n- [ ] 8.3 Run `E2E_DB_PORT=15433 pnpm test:e2e -- e2e/web` against the new image and verify chat and search specs behave as before (CI is the arbiter for pass/fail on this box)\n\n## 9. Documentation\n\n- [ ] 9.1 Add the dated `CHANGELOG.md` entry covering the embedding layer and the BREAKING database-image requirement, and verify `pnpm lint:markdown` passes\n- [ ] 9.2 Document the operator surface — declaring an embedding model, running backfill, reading coverage, and the staged model-migration order — in `apps/api/AGENTS.md`, and verify the config example in `llame.config.json.example` loads\n- [ ] 9.3 Run `openspec validate add-chat-search-embeddings --strict` and confirm the change is ready to archive\n",
