hunk, on a corpus proportional to conversation volume.\n- The generated line is **untrusted derived text**: it is produced by a model reading user content and must be framed and escaped accordingly wherever it surfaces.\n- Regeneration and invalidation ride the existing `embed_input_version` mechanism from #196: changing what is embedded is an enumerable re-embed, never a silent divergence.\n- Bulk generation is explicit, never a side effect of enabling it — same rule #196 establishes for backfill.\n\n## Boundaries\n\nNot scheduled, and explicitly **after** #196 and #197. The deterministic anchor from #517 must be measured first: without a baseline that includes it, there is no way to tell what the model-generated version actually bought over a free heuristic. Cost per chunk, an extra provider dependency, and a second class of model-authored text in the retrieval path all need to be justified by a measured lift on the eval dataset, not assumed.\n\nThis is not chunk summarization for display, not conversation summarization (compaction already owns that, SPEC §2.1), and not a replacement for verbatim storage — the projection remains derived from canonical messages.\n\n## Cross-links\n\n- #517 ships the deterministic anchor this would generalize.\n- #196 owns `embed_input_version`, the mechanism that makes changing embedding input safe.\n- #197 owns the eval baseline any lift must be measured against.\n- Recorded as an open question in `openspec/changes/add-chat-search-embeddings/design.md` (D11, D13).\n\nRefs #194.\nEOF\ngh issue create --title \"feat(api): model-generated chunk context for embedding input (contextual retrieval)\" --body-file $S/issueB.md --label enhancement --label knowledge --label future 2>&1 | tail -3",
