            "command": "cd /home/leon0399/.herdr/worktrees/llame/episodic-recall/openspec/changes/add-chat-search-embeddings\npython3 - <<'PY'\n# ---- instance-config spec: batch size field ----\np='specs/instance-config/spec.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"Each entry MAY include a distance metric, a model revision, and optional asymmetric `documentPrefix` / `queryPrefix` strings.\",\n\"Each entry MAY include a distance metric, a model revision, a positive-integer `batchSize` bounding how many documents are sent per provider request, and optional asymmetric `documentPrefix` / `queryPrefix` strings.\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\n# ---- proposal ----\np='proposal.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- A **per-corpus embedding store** for chat chunks, holding one vector per (document, model) so model generations coexist, with denormalized owner and chat columns and RLS `ENABLE` + `FORCE` and no public-read — the same isolation invariants the lexical projection already carries.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Embeddings as nullable columns on the existing projection table** — vector, model key, embedded content hash, input version, and failure reason — so a document is at most one vector and tenant isolation is inherited rather than restated. One model serves a corpus at a time; a model change re-embeds in place. (Design decision D2 — this replaces the separate embedding table sketched on #196, whose only justification was a parallel two-model migration nobody asked for.)\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- A **content-hash validity rule**: an embedding is valid only while its recorded content hash still matches the projection row it describes. Results that arrive after the underlying content was edited or deleted are dropped, never applied, so a late provider response can never restore deleted content.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- A **content-hash validity rule**: an embedding is valid only while its recorded content hash and input version still match the document. Results arriving after the content was edited or deleted are dropped, never applied, so a late provider response can never restore deleted content — and a rebuild clears the embedding in the same statement that rewrites content.\n- **Terminal failures recorded in place** so a permanently unembeddable document is neither retried forever nor silently hidden, superseded automatically when content, input version, or model changes, and clearable by an operator command.\n- **No completeness gate.** Retrieval fuses whatever legs exist — a partially embedded corpus is fully searchable, with the vector leg contributing where vectors are present. A per-row model-key filter keeps two embedding spaces from ever meeting in one ranking.\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- **Model-migration discipline**: register a new model, backfill in parallel, evaluate against the recorded eval baseline, activate, retire the old vectors after a safe period. Vectors are never overwritten in place; a provider change is a new internal key.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **A fourth worker group, `search-embed`**, so embedding concurrency — which is the provider spend and saturation dial — is an operator setting rather than a source constant, and so network-bound embedding does not share a concurrency number or a retry policy with DB-bound lexical rebuilds.\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- **Schema:** new migration adding the model registry and the chat-chunk vector store, the vector store under FORCE RLS with no public-read (the ledger is instance-global operator state and carries no tenant column, so no RLS), plus a BYPASSRLS-owned coverage-discovery function alongside the existing lexical one. Cross-tenant negatives live in a `*-rls.integration.test.ts` suite alongside the existing ones.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Schema:** one migration adding the `vector` extension, five nullable embedding columns on `search_chat_documents`, a model-binding ledger (instance-global operator state, no tenant column, so no RLS), and a BYPASSRLS-owned coverage-discovery function alongside the existing lexical one. Isolation is inherited from the projection's existing FORCE-RLS policy; cross-tenant negatives are extended to cover the embedding columns explicitly.\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- **Code:** `apps/api/src/search/core/` gains the corpus-agnostic backend interface and adapters; a chat-scoped embedding worker joins the existing reindex worker and queue definitions in `apps/api/src/search/`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Code:** `apps/api/src/search/core/` gains the corpus-agnostic backend interface and one OpenAI-compatible adapter; an embed worker and queue join the existing reindex worker in `apps/api/src/search/`. `SearchModule` stays a leaf — it imports no new module. `WORKER_GROUPS` gains `search-embed`, with matching config-schema, profile, and `docs/scaling.md` updates.\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- **Operations:** a new queue and worker to observe, a backfill to run once per existing instance, and one new outbound provider dependency when configured.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Operations:** a new queue, worker, and worker group to observe; three operator commands (`backfill`, `prune`, `retry-failed`); per-chat coverage reported as distinct embedded/failed/outstanding counts; and one new outbound provider dependency when configured.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nPY\nopenspec validate add-chat-search-embeddings --strict 2>&1 | tail -2",
