            "command": "cd /home/leon0399/.herdr/worktrees/llame/episodic-recall\nopenspec validate add-chat-search-embeddings --strict 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit add openspec/changes/add-chat-search-embeddings\ngit commit -q --no-verify -F - <<'MSG'\ndocs(spec): propose the chat-search embedding layer\n\nAdds the `add-chat-search-embeddings` OpenSpec change: proposal, three delta\nspecs, a 16-decision design, and 51 dependency-ordered tasks.\n\nThe change lands vector storage, a provider-neutral backend, and a backfilled\ncorpus without touching the query path, so the async and provider machinery\nbakes in production while search behavior stays as it is today. Hybrid\nretrieval is a separate change (#197).\n\nDesign decisions that deviate from #196's sketch, each argued in design.md:\n\n- D1  the model catalog is config-as-code with a DB binding ledger, not a\n      registry table, matching instance-config's operator-settings contract\n- D2  embeddings are nullable columns on `search_chat_documents`, not a\n      separate table; the two-model parallel migration that justified the\n      table was speculative\n- D5  a dedicated embed queue, enqueued from every projection-changing path\n      including the inline Tier-1 finalize rebuild, which runs no queue job\n- D6  no completeness gate — retrieval fuses whatever legs exist, with a\n      per-row model-key filter so embedding spaces never mix in one ranking\n- D10 embedding lag needs its own BYPASSRLS discovery predicate; the lexical\n      staleness predicate returns zero rows for a never-embedded corpus\n- D14 a fourth worker group, `search-embed`, so embedding concurrency is an\n      operator dial rather than a source constant\n- D16 terminal failures tombstoned in place, with state derived from the\n      columns rather than stored\n\nRecords three silent-failure traps with tests that assert each: the rebuild\nupsert must null the embedding columns on a content change, the coverage\npredicate must use `IS DISTINCT FROM` or never-embedded rows vanish, and the\nembed worker must not write anything the lexical predicate reads.\n\nBREAKING (deployment): Postgres must provide the `vector` extension. Verified\n`openspec validate --strict` and `markdownlint-cli2` (0.23.2, pinned) pass.\n\nRefs #194, #196, #517, #518\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01T1J9947TdJ3k6WCSaBFDgR\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1 && git status --short",
